# nr-tui-entry-argv: the new crate mixdog-entry (native/core/crates/mixdog-entry, `[[bin]] name = "mixdog"`) and one library function added to
# mixdog-cli (native/core/crates/mixdog-cli/src/exec/mod.rs). Nothing was compiled: the crate is not a workspace member yet.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace] members
Add, after "crates/mixdog-cli" (the crate depends on mixdog-cli and mixdog-launch, both already members):
    "crates/mixdog-entry",

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies] (internal crates)
mixdog-cli is not a workspace dependency yet (the crate names it `mixdog-cli = { workspace = true }`). Add beside the other path crates:
    mixdog-cli = { path = "crates/mixdog-cli" }
mixdog-entry itself needs no entry: nothing depends on it.

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock
Regenerate (`cargo update --workspace --offline`): one new package `mixdog-entry`. Every dependency is already in the lock:
mixdog-cli, mixdog-core, mixdog-launch, mixdog-js, serde_json, mixdog-workspace-hack; dev: mixdog-testkit, httparse, flate2, rcgen, rustls,
tempfile, tokio, tokio-rustls, regex, uuid, mixdog-ai, windows-sys (windows). No crate is added to the lock.

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
`cargo hakari generate` after (1): the crate carries `mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }` already.

## 5. dev-dependency feature unification
mixdog-entry's [dev-dependencies] list mixdog-ai with its four test-only features (`count-work`, `replay-bytes`, `test-support`,
`virtual-clock`): `test-support` is what makes the binary honour REPLAY_PROVIDER_PIN in tests/exec_entry.rs. Run
D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py after (1): if it wants the other lines of mixdog-cli's dev-dependency block (mixdog-core,
mixdog-services, mixdog-exthost ... with their test-only features) for this crate, let it write them; they do not change what the test needs.

## 6. compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: the crate registers no protocol method.

## 7. mixdog-cli/src/main.rs (the lead's, with the exthost track's edits): one implementation of the exec run
This task moved the body of `exec_command` that starts after the argument check into the library as `exec::run_command(options: ExecOptions) -> i32`
(it validates the explicit route, prints `mixdog: <refusal>` and returns 1, else resolves the JS runtime and data folder, boots the executors,
reads the credentials and runs the exec on its own thread; the code is the exec's exit code), with `exec::StdSink` for the sink. `mixdogd exec` and `mixdog exec`
must not each keep a copy: in main.rs
  - delete `struct StdSink` and its `impl exec::Sink` (the library has it);
  - in `exec_command`, `Ok(exec::Invocation::Run(options))` becomes the arm that runs: `return ExitCode::from(u8::try_from(exec::run_command(options)).unwrap_or(1));`
    (the route check moves into run_command; `Plain` and `Err(refusal)` keep printing `mixdog: <text>` as now),
  - delete everything after that match (the `let js = ...` block down to `ExitCode::from(u8::try_from(code).unwrap_or(1))`) and the `use` lines that only it needed
    (`Arc`, `TaskClass`, if nothing else in main.rs uses them: `migrate` still uses both).
Until that edit lands both binaries run the same exec; main.rs's own copy is the only duplicate and is removed by it.

## 8. Not shipped
tests/exec_entry.rs covers the six exec cases of fixtures/exec-cli that need only this binary; `beside-daemon` stays in mixdog-cli's exec_cli_replay.rs
(it starts `mixdogd serve`). interactive.rs is the stub the switch task (nr-tui-switch) replaces; the binary is not packaged before that.
